-- CA_0173_la_city_by_district_batch_d2_2026.sql
-- LA-cities slice, by-district batch D2: El Monte, Glendora, Diamond Bar, Claremont, La Verne. All five elect their
-- council BY DISTRICT but were modeled at large; each gets one LOCAL district row + X0001 polygon per council district
-- (LA RR/CC precinct layer, Political_Boundaries/MapServer/34, DST_CITY/DIV_CITY, dissolved; read 2026-09-23; QA:
-- districts cover each TIGER place polygon 0.996-0.9995, seam-only overlaps -- the CA_0141/CA_0167/CA_0172 method),
-- and each sitting member's EXISTING office moves onto their district (term history moves with it). District
-- assignment = each city's own council page / notice of nominees, read 2026-09-22/23.
-- Council-chosen mayors: the member the 2025 roster import put in a separate "Mayor" office is simply that district's
-- member (Fredendall D2, Teng D4, Calaycay D1, Hepburn D4). El Monte's Mayor is elected at large and stays citywide.
--
-- MISSING MEMBERS (the 2025 CA Roster import left out the 2026 mayor in three cities) are seated on a new district seat:
--   Diamond Bar  D1  Steve Tye            https://www.diamondbarca.gov/262/City-Council
--   Claremont    D3  Jennifer Stark       https://www.claremontca.gov/Government/City-Council
--   La Verne     D1  Steven F. Johnson    https://www.laverneca.gov/351/City-Council
--
-- EL MONTE CLERK / TREASURER: both elected; neither office existed. Created on the Mayor's LOCAL_EXEC district (Carson
-- pattern) with holders Gabriel Ramirez (City Clerk) and Hannah M. Caceres (City Treasurer, sworn in 2025-01-27, not
-- a 2026 candidate).
--
-- CONTESTS (each clerk's list, verified name by name and district by district against the original):
--   El Monte Mayor                            3 candidate(s)  1 incumbent(s)
--   El Monte City Council District 2          1 candidate(s)  1 incumbent(s)  (uncontested)
--   El Monte City Council District 3          1 candidate(s)  1 incumbent(s)  (uncontested)
--   El Monte City Council District 6          2 candidate(s)  1 incumbent(s)
--   El Monte City Clerk                       2 candidate(s)  1 incumbent(s)
--   El Monte City Treasurer                   3 candidate(s)  0 incumbent(s)
--   Glendora City Council District 1          2 candidate(s)  1 incumbent(s)
--   Glendora City Council District 4          3 candidate(s)  1 incumbent(s)
--   Diamond Bar City Council District 1       2 candidate(s)  1 incumbent(s)
--   Diamond Bar City Council District 3       1 candidate(s)  1 incumbent(s)  (uncontested)
--   Diamond Bar City Council District 4       2 candidate(s)  1 incumbent(s)
--   Claremont City Council District 2         1 candidate(s)  1 incumbent(s)  (uncontested)
--   Claremont City Council District 3         2 candidate(s)  1 incumbent(s)
--   Claremont City Council District 4         3 candidate(s)  0 incumbent(s)
--   La Verne City Council District 1          2 candidate(s)  1 incumbent(s)
--   La Verne City Council District 3          2 candidate(s)  1 incumbent(s)
--   La Verne City Council District 4          1 candidate(s)  1 incumbent(s)  (uncontested)
-- Uncontested district seats stay on the ballot as far as the city record shows (no EC 10229 appointment found: El
-- Monte D2/D3, Diamond Bar D3, Claremont D2, La Verne D4). Mayor Pro Tem Longoria (El Monte D4) runs for Mayor as a
-- sitting official, not the seat incumbent.
--
-- RACES go on '2026 LA County General' (d91a20ce-557e-4615-a31b-5b2b3df2ed14); primary_party NULL; no party stored.
-- IDEMPOTENT: fixed ids for every new row; office moves guarded on the target; every insert NOT EXISTS-guarded.

